BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-levers@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261019T173000
DTEND:20261019T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: The Magic Fork
DESCRIPTION:"I bet you can lift this big heavy book with ONE finger. Want
  to see how?"\n\nGrab:\n- ruler or paint stirrer\n- thick marker or roun
 d pencil (the pivot)\n- a heavy-ish book\n- a few toy cars or blocks\n\n
 https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/levers.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/levers.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-drop-race@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261022T173000
DTEND:20261022T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Drop Race
DESCRIPTION:"If I drop a big heavy book and a tiny little ball at the sam
 e time\, which one wins?"\n\nGrab:\n- a hardcover book\n- a small ball\n
 - a sheet of paper\n- a soft landing spot (rug or pillow)\n\nhttps://tim
 jfarrell.com/stem-lab/drop-race.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/drop-race.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-ramps@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261026T173000
DTEND:20261026T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Ramp Racers
DESCRIPTION:"Can we make a car go super far without pushing it at all?"\n
 \nGrab:\n- a board\, baking sheet or big book (the ramp)\n- pillows or b
 ooks to prop it\n- two or three toy cars\n- painter's tape or a sock to 
 mark where they stop\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/ramps.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/ramps.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-patterns@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261029T173000
DTEND:20261029T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Pattern Snakes
DESCRIPTION:"I'm going to make a snake\, and it has a secret code. Can yo
 u crack it?"\n\nGrab:\n- two kinds of pasta\, or two colors of blocks\, 
 LEGO or crayons\n- a string (optional\, for threading pasta)\n\nhttps://
 timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/patterns.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/patterns.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-sink-float@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261102T173000
DTEND:20261102T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Sink or Float?
DESCRIPTION:"Some things swim and some things sink. Let's be scientists a
 nd guess first."\n\nGrab:\n- a big bowl or the bathtub\n- a towel\n- 6 t
 o 10 things: apple\, grape\, coin\, cork\, spoon\, LEGO\, crayon\, toy b
 oat\, orange (with and without peel)\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab
 /sink-float.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/sink-float.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-balance-scale@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261105T173000
DTEND:20261105T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Hanger Scale
DESCRIPTION:"Let's build a machine that tells us which thing is heavier\,
  no guessing allowed."\n\nGrab:\n- a coat hanger with notches or a plain
  hanger\n- two paper or plastic cups\n- string or tape\n- a door handle 
 or cabinet knob to hang it from\n- small things to weigh: blocks\, crayo
 ns\, coins\, grapes\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/balance-scale.ht
 ml
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/balance-scale.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-shadows@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261109T173000
DTEND:20261109T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Shadow Monsters
DESCRIPTION:"Let's turn the lights off and make a monster that's bigger t
 han the whole family."\n\nGrab:\n- a flashlight or phone light\n- a blan
 k wall\n- hands\, a toy figure\, a fork\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-
 lab/shadows.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/shadows.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-triangles@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261112T173000
DTEND:20261112T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Strong Shapes
DESCRIPTION:"Builders have a favorite shape that makes bridges and towers
  super strong. Let's find out which one."\n\nGrab:\n- straws or pipe cle
 aners\n- play-dough\, mini marshmallows or tape for corners\n- a toy to 
 test with\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/triangles.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/triangles.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-magnets@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261116T173000
DTEND:20261116T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Magnet Hunt
DESCRIPTION:"This magnet has a secret power. It only likes some things. L
 et's find out which."\n\nGrab:\n- a big fridge magnet (or a magnet wand)
 \n- a tray of things: spoon\, foil\, coin\, paper clip\, key\, LEGO\, a 
 steel food can and an aluminum soda can\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-
 lab/magnets.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/magnets.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-rubber-band-guitar@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261119T173000
DTEND:20261119T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Box Guitar
DESCRIPTION:"Let's make a guitar out of junk and find out where sound com
 es from."\n\nGrab:\n- a tissue box or shoebox with a hole cut in the lid
 \n- 4 rubber bands\, thick and thin\n- a pencil to lift the strings\n\nh
 ttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/rubber-band-guitar.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/rubber-band-guitar.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-friction@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261123T173000
DTEND:20261123T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Slippy and Grippy
DESCRIPTION:"Why can you slide in socks on the floor but not on the rug?"
 \n\nGrab:\n- the ramp from Ramp Racers\n- a toy car or a block\n- three 
 ramp coverings: a towel\, foil or wax paper\, sandpaper or a bath mat\n\
 nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/friction.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/friction.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-measuring@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261130T173000
DTEND:20261130T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: How Many Hands?
DESCRIPTION:"How long is the couch? Not in inches. In YOUR hands."\n\nGra
 b:\n- their hands and feet\n- your hands and feet\n- a toy or a LEGO bri
 ck as another unit\n- a tape measure for the end\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.
 com/stem-lab/measuring.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/measuring.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-balloon-rocket@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261203T173000
DTEND:20261203T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Balloon Rocket
DESCRIPTION:"We're going to launch a rocket across the room. Fuel: air."\
 n\nGrab:\n- a balloon\n- a long string (about 3 m)\n- a straw\n- tape\n-
  two chairs\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/balloon-rocket.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/balloon-rocket.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-dissolving@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261207T173000
DTEND:20261207T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Where Did It Go?
DESCRIPTION:"I can make sugar disappear. Want to see?"\n\nGrab:\n- 4 clea
 r glasses of water\n- spoon\n- sugar\, salt\, sand or dirt\, and a littl
 e rice or a LEGO\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/dissolving.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/dissolving.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-pendulum@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261210T173000
DTEND:20261210T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Sock Swing
DESCRIPTION:"Let's make a swing for a toy and see if we can make it go fa
 ster."\n\nGrab:\n- a long string\n- a sock with a small toy or a few coi
 ns tied inside\n- a table edge or doorway to hang it from\n\nhttps://tim
 jfarrell.com/stem-lab/pendulum.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/pendulum.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-symmetry@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261214T173000
DTEND:20261214T174500
SUMMARY:Lab: Paint Butterflies
DESCRIPTION:"I'm going to paint only half a butterfly\, and the paper wil
 l paint the other half for me."\n\nGrab:\n- paper\n- washable paint\n- a
  small mirror (optional)\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/symmetry.ht
 ml
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/symmetry.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-pulleys@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261217T173000
DTEND:20261217T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Broomstick Superpower
DESCRIPTION:"Can you pull two grown-ups across the room all by yourself? 
 Let's find out."\n\nGrab:\n- two broom handles or mop handles\n- a rope 
 about 4 m long\n- a second grown-up (or tie one broom to a heavy table l
 eg)\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/pulleys.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/pulleys.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stem-lab-rainbows@tradlab
DTSTAMP:20261015T214244Z
DTSTART:20261221T173000
DTEND:20261221T174000
SUMMARY:Lab: Rainbow Maker
DESCRIPTION:"White light has a secret. There's a rainbow hiding inside it
 ."\n\nGrab:\n- a clear glass of water\n- a flashlight or a sunny window\
 n- white paper\n- an old CD if you have one\n\nhttps://timjfarrell.com/s
 tem-lab/rainbows.html
URL:https://timjfarrell.com/stem-lab/rainbows.html
END:VEVENT
